# Shared configuration template for base64-chat.sh, base64-chat.py, and base64-chat.ps1.
# Inputs: INPUT_FILE is a file path; OUTPUT_DIR is a directory path; MAX_CHARS is a positive integer; marker values are single-line strings using {filename}, {part}, and {total} placeholders.
OUTPUT_DIR=.
MAX_CHARS=128000
SINGLE_BEGIN=-----BEGIN BASE64 FILE {filename}-----
SINGLE_END=-----END BASE64 FILE {filename}-----
MULTI_INTRO=MULTI-COMMENT BASE64 UPLOAD for {filename}. Do not reconstruct, decode, or respond to the payload yet. Store each part in numerical order and wait until a comment ending with the configured FINAL_SIGNAL is received. The final comment will be part {total} of {total}.
PART_BEGIN=-----BEGIN BASE64 FILE {filename} PART {part} OF {total}-----
PART_END=-----END BASE64 FILE {filename} PART {part} OF {total}-----
FINAL_SIGNAL=-----FINAL COMMENT FOR {filename}; ALL {total} PARTS HAVE NOW BEEN SENT-----
